---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { AMAZON_DISCLOSURE, AMAZON_TAG, ASINS } from '../config/affiliate';
import { models } from '../data/models';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { crumbLd, webPageLd } from '../lib/ld';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Affiliate disclosure', path: '/affiliate-disclosure/' }];
const desc = 'Amazon Associates disclosure for TreadmillSpecs.com. Links use tag treadmillspecs-20. Direct product links are only for ASINs checked on a live Amazon page. No prices are shown.';
const verified = Object.entries(ASINS).map(([slug, row]) => {
  const model = models.find((m) => m.slug === slug);
  return { name: model?.name ?? row.label, title: row.title, asin: row.asin };
});
const jsonld = [webPageLd('Affiliate disclosure', '/affiliate-disclosure/', desc, SITE.checked), crumbLd(crumbs)];
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description={desc} path="/affiliate-disclosure/" og="/og/page-affiliate-disclosure.png" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <Crumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
      <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    </div>
    <p>{AMAZON_DISCLOSURE}</p>
    <p>TreadmillSpecs.com participates in the Amazon Associates Program. Amazon is the only affiliate program on this site. There are no display ads and no other merchant links. Every Amazon link is built in one configuration file. The tag is <span class="mono">{AMAZON_TAG}</span>.</p>
    <h2>Two kinds of link</h2>
    <p>A <span class="mono">/dp/</span> link is used only when that Amazon product page was opened on 1 November 2026 and the title named that one model. {verified.length} models passed that check:</p>
    <ul>
      {verified.map((row) => <li>{row.name}. Amazon title: “{row.title}.” ASIN {row.asin}.</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>The other models use a tagged Amazon search, because the live results were a multi-model family, a different machine, or a title that did not name the model. A search is not a promise that the first result is the treadmill on the spec page. Opening a search or a product page can set cookies on Amazon’s site. This site does not read those cookies.</p>
    <h2>What the links do not change</h2>
    <p>No prices are shown. A spec cell is filled from the manufacturer page or manual before a shopping link is added. A missing spec is not filled because a retailer page, or an Amazon title, mentions a number. The BowFlex T16 title includes a horsepower phrase. The BowFlex spec block does not, so the motor cell stays unpublished while the product link remains.</p>
    <p>The tag does not change which model wins a footprint sort, a height sort, or a written comparison. Those pages use the manufacturer inches. If you follow a link and buy something, Amazon may pay a commission. That commission does not add a row to a table.</p>
    <p>Questions about a link go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
